From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:28:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avdevice/v4l2: add DRM PRIME output

A capture device and a hardware consumer usually share memory: the
driver writes the image into a DMA-BUF-capable buffer, and a scaler or
encoder can read that buffer where it lies. The v4l2 input device hands
every frame out as system memory, so reaching such a consumer costs a
copy per frame, and at 4K60 in RGB that is some 1.5 GB/s of memory
traffic spent moving pixels nobody changes.

Add a drm_prime option. With it set, each capture buffer is exported
once with VIDIOC_EXPBUF, and each dequeued buffer is handed out as a
DRM PRIME frame referencing it, in a wrapped_avframe packet, the way
kmsgrab hands out scanout buffers. The frames context takes the capture
format as its software format, so hwdownload brings a frame to system
memory, and a hardware filter or encoder imports the buffer directly.
A buffer returns to the driver when the last reference to its frame is
released. The drm_device option names the DRM device the frames context
is created on; nothing is allocated from it.

The plane layout comes from the driver's own format rather than from
the frame dimensions. Some receivers pad each line: the Synopsys HDMI RX
driver aligns every line to 64 bytes, so a 1366-pixel NV12 line is 1408
bytes long. Taking the pitch from bytesperline and the image size from
sizeimage describes such a buffer correctly.

The copying path falls back to copying when too few buffers remain
queued. A frame that references its buffer has no such fallback, so in
this mode the frame is dropped and its buffer re-queued at once,
through FFERROR_REDO, which keeps the driver capturing the newest image.
A consumer that holds too many frames loses frames instead of stalling
capture. One that has to hold more frames than the driver granted
buffers before releasing any is never handed another frame, so the
first drop is a warning, and the count is logged at close. The margin
needs a third buffer, so fewer than three is refused.

In this mode the stream's forced codec is wrapped_avframe, because
stream probing opens the decoder that names; leaving the raw codec there
made probing try a rawvideo decoder on wrapped frames.

Supported are the single-plane formats that the device's format table
maps and that have a DRM equivalent: NV12, NV16, NV24, YUYV, UYVY, BGR24
and RGB24. The mode needs libdrm and cannot be combined with libv4l2,
whose conversions happen in buffers of its own.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 doc/indevs.texi    |  32 ++++
 libavdevice/v4l2.c | 402 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 409 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/indevs.texi b/doc/indevs.texi
index 8822e07..29cfcde 100644
--- a/doc/indevs.texi
+++ b/doc/indevs.texi
@@ -1370,6 +1370,14 @@ frame rate and size as previously set:
 @example
 ffmpeg -f video4linux2 -input_format mjpeg -i /dev/video0 out.mpeg
 @end example
+
+@item
+Grab without copying and bring the frames to system memory, to check what a
+hardware consumer would be handed:
+@example
+ffmpeg -f video4linux2 -drm_prime 1 -input_format nv12 -i /dev/video0 \
+       -vf hwdownload,format=nv12 -f framemd5 -
+@end example
 @end itemize
 
 For more information about Video4Linux, check @url{http://linuxtv.org/}.
@@ -1446,6 +1454,30 @@ Default value is @code{default}.
 @item use_libv4l2
 Use libv4l2 (v4l-utils) conversion functions. Default is 0.
 
+@item drm_prime
+Output @code{drm_prime} frames that reference the capture buffers instead
+of copying them, so a hardware filter or encoder reads the captured image
+where the driver wrote it. The stream is @code{wrapped_avframe}, and the
+frames context takes the capture format as its software format. Each buffer
+is exported once, as a DMA-BUF, when capture starts. A buffer returns to the
+driver when the last reference to its frame is released.
+
+A consumer that holds so many frames that too few buffers remain queued
+loses the frames captured meanwhile rather than stalling capture. The first
+dropped frame is a warning, and the count is logged at close. A consumer that
+has to hold more frames than the driver granted buffers before it releases
+any is never handed another frame; download the frames to system memory
+before such a filter.
+
+The capture format must be a single memory plane in one of
+@code{nv12}, @code{nv16}, @code{nv24}, @code{yuyv422}, @code{uyvy422},
+@code{bgr24} or @code{rgb24}. It cannot be combined with
+@option{use_libv4l2}, and it needs at least three buffers. Default is 0.
+
+@item drm_device
+The DRM device the @code{drm_prime} frames context is created on. Nothing is
+allocated from it. Default is @file{/dev/dri/renderD128}.
+
 @end table
 
 @section vfwcap
diff --git a/libavdevice/v4l2.c b/libavdevice/v4l2.c
index a51fc70..09af2ff 100644
--- a/libavdevice/v4l2.c
+++ b/libavdevice/v4l2.c
@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@
 #include <libv4l2.h>
 #endif
 
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+#include <drm_fourcc.h>
+#include "libavutil/hwcontext.h"
+#include "libavutil/hwcontext_drm.h"
+#endif
+
 static const int desired_video_buffers = 256;
 
 #define V4L_ALLFORMATS  3
@@ -107,6 +113,16 @@ struct video_data {
     int list_standard;  /**< Set by a private option. */
     char *framerate;    /**< Set by a private option. */
 
+    int drm_prime;      /**< Set by a private option. */
+    char *drm_device;   /**< Set by a private option. */
+    int *dmabuf_fd;     /**< Exported buffer per index, in DRM PRIME mode. */
+    unsigned int frames_dropped;
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+    AVBufferRef *device_ref;
+    AVBufferRef *frames_ref;
+    AVDRMLayerDescriptor drm_layer;
+#endif
+
     int use_libv4l2;
     int (*open_f)(const char *file, int oflag, ...);
     int (*close_f)(int fd);
@@ -376,6 +392,13 @@ static int mmap_init(AVFormatContext *ctx)
         av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Insufficient buffer memory\n");
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
     }
+    /* One buffer stays queued and one is the low-water margin, so a frame
+     * can only be handed out when a third exists. */
+    if (s->drm_prime && req.count < 3) {
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "DRM PRIME output needs at least 3 buffers, "
+               "the driver granted %u\n", req.count);
+        return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+    }
     s->buffers = req.count;
     s->buf_start = av_malloc_array(s->buffers, sizeof(void *));
     if (!s->buf_start) {
@@ -388,6 +411,17 @@ static int mmap_init(AVFormatContext *ctx)
         av_freep(&s->buf_start);
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
     }
+    if (s->drm_prime) {
+        s->dmabuf_fd = av_malloc_array(s->buffers, sizeof(int));
+        if (!s->dmabuf_fd) {
+            av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Cannot allocate buffer descriptors\n");
+            av_freep(&s->buf_start);
+            av_freep(&s->buf_len);
+            return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+        }
+        for (i = 0; i < s->buffers; i++)
+            s->dmabuf_fd[i] = -1;
+    }
 
     for (i = 0; i < req.count; i++) {
         unsigned int buf_length, buf_offset;
@@ -424,6 +458,30 @@ static int mmap_init(AVFormatContext *ctx)
                    i, s->buf_len[i], s->frame_size);
             return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
         }
+
+        if (s->drm_prime) {
+            /* The frames reference the buffer itself, so it is exported
+             * rather than mapped. The fd stays open until close and every
+             * frame of this index shares it. A consumer only reads a
+             * captured frame, so the export is read-only. */
+            struct v4l2_exportbuffer expbuf = {
+                .type  = s->buf_type,
+                .index = i,
+                .plane = 0,
+                .flags = O_RDONLY,
+            };
+
+            s->buf_start[i] = NULL;
+            if (v4l2_ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_EXPBUF, &expbuf) < 0) {
+                res = AVERROR(errno);
+                av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "ioctl(VIDIOC_EXPBUF): %s\n",
+                       av_err2str(res));
+                return res;
+            }
+            s->dmabuf_fd[i] = expbuf.fd;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         s->buf_start[i] = v4l2_mmap(NULL, buf_length,
                                PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED,
                                s->fd, buf_offset);
@@ -452,27 +510,131 @@ static int enqueue_buffer(struct video_data *s, struct v4l2_buffer *buf)
     return res;
 }
 
-static void mmap_release_buffer(void *opaque, uint8_t *data)
+static int requeue_buffer(struct video_data *s, int index)
 {
     struct v4l2_plane planes[VIDEO_MAX_PLANES];
-    struct v4l2_buffer buf = { 0 };
+    struct v4l2_buffer buf = {
+        .type     = s->buf_type,
+        .memory   = V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP,
+        .index    = index,
+        .m.planes = s->multiplanar ? planes : NULL,
+        .length   = s->multiplanar ? VIDEO_MAX_PLANES : 0,
+    };
+
+    /* A packet can outlive the device: the framework frees the packets it
+     * buffered after read_close. Such a buffer has no queue to return to. */
+    if (s->fd < 0)
+        return 0;
+
+    return enqueue_buffer(s, &buf);
+}
+
+static void mmap_release_buffer(void *opaque, uint8_t *data)
+{
     struct buff_data *buf_descriptor = opaque;
     struct video_data *s = buf_descriptor->s;
+    int index = buf_descriptor->index;
 
-    buf.type = s->buf_type;
-    buf.memory = V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP;
-    buf.index = buf_descriptor->index;
-    buf.m.planes = s->multiplanar ? planes : NULL;
-    buf.length   = s->multiplanar ? VIDEO_MAX_PLANES : 0;
     av_free(buf_descriptor);
+    requeue_buffer(s, index);
+}
 
-    /* A packet can outlive the device: the framework frees the packets it
-     * buffered after read_close. Such a buffer has no queue to return to. */
-    if (s->fd < 0)
-        return;
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+static const struct {
+    uint32_t v4l2_fmt;
+    uint32_t drm_fmt;
+    enum AVPixelFormat sw_fmt;
+} drm_prime_formats[] = {
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12,  DRM_FORMAT_NV12,   AV_PIX_FMT_NV12    },
+#ifdef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV16
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV16,  DRM_FORMAT_NV16,   AV_PIX_FMT_NV16    },
+#endif
+#ifdef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV24
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV24,  DRM_FORMAT_NV24,   AV_PIX_FMT_NV24    },
+#endif
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV,  DRM_FORMAT_YUYV,   AV_PIX_FMT_YUYV422 },
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_UYVY,  DRM_FORMAT_UYVY,   AV_PIX_FMT_UYVY422 },
+    /* V4L2 names the byte order, DRM the little-endian word: both are B, G, R
+     * in memory. */
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_BGR24, DRM_FORMAT_RGB888, AV_PIX_FMT_BGR24   },
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_RGB24, DRM_FORMAT_BGR888, AV_PIX_FMT_RGB24   },
+};
+
+static void drm_prime_release_buffer(void *opaque, uint8_t *data)
+{
+    av_free(data);
+    mmap_release_buffer(opaque, NULL);
+}
+
+static void drm_prime_free_frame(void *opaque, uint8_t *data)
+{
+    AVFrame *frame = (AVFrame *)data;
+
+    av_frame_free(&frame);
+}
+
+/**
+ * Wrap a dequeued buffer in a DRM PRIME frame and hand it out as a
+ * wrapped-AVFrame packet. The buffer goes back to the driver when the frame
+ * is freed, or here if wrapping fails, so the caller never re-queues it.
+ */
+static int drm_prime_wrap_buffer(AVFormatContext *ctx, AVPacket *pkt, int index)
+{
+    struct video_data *s = ctx->priv_data;
+    AVDRMFrameDescriptor *desc = av_mallocz(sizeof(*desc));
+    struct buff_data *buf_descriptor = av_malloc(sizeof(*buf_descriptor));
+    AVFrame *frame = av_frame_alloc();
+
+    if (!desc || !buf_descriptor || !frame)
+        goto fail;
+
+    desc->nb_objects                = 1;
+    desc->objects[0].fd             = s->dmabuf_fd[index];
+    desc->objects[0].size           = s->buf_len[index];
+    desc->objects[0].format_modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+    desc->nb_layers                 = 1;
+    desc->layers[0]                 = s->drm_layer;
+
+    buf_descriptor->index = index;
+    buf_descriptor->s     = s;
 
-    enqueue_buffer(s, &buf);
+    frame->buf[0] = av_buffer_create((uint8_t *)desc, sizeof(*desc),
+                                     drm_prime_release_buffer, buf_descriptor, 0);
+    if (!frame->buf[0])
+        goto fail;
+    desc           = NULL;
+    buf_descriptor = NULL;
+
+    frame->hw_frames_ctx = av_buffer_ref(s->frames_ref);
+    if (!frame->hw_frames_ctx)
+        goto fail_frame;
+    frame->data[0] = frame->buf[0]->data;
+    frame->format  = AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME;
+    frame->width   = s->width;
+    frame->height  = s->height;
+
+    pkt->buf = av_buffer_create((uint8_t *)frame, sizeof(*frame),
+                                drm_prime_free_frame, NULL, 0);
+    if (!pkt->buf)
+        goto fail_frame;
+    pkt->data   = (uint8_t *)frame;
+    pkt->size   = sizeof(*frame);
+    pkt->flags |= AV_PKT_FLAG_TRUSTED;
+
+    return 0;
+
+fail:
+    av_free(desc);
+    av_free(buf_descriptor);
+    av_frame_free(&frame);
+    requeue_buffer(s, index);
+    return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+fail_frame:
+    /* The frame owns the buffer now, so freeing it re-queues the buffer. */
+    av_frame_free(&frame);
+    return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
 }
+#endif
 
 #if HAVE_CLOCK_GETTIME && defined(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
 static int64_t av_gettime_monotonic(void)
@@ -597,6 +759,41 @@ static int mmap_read_frame(AVFormatContext *ctx, AVPacket *pkt)
         }
     }
 
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+    if (s->drm_prime) {
+        /* A frame references its buffer until it is freed, so there is no
+         * copy to fall back on when the queue runs low. The frame is dropped
+         * instead, which keeps the driver capturing the newest image: a
+         * consumer that holds too many frames loses frames rather than
+         * stalling capture. One that holds more than the margin leaves
+         * before releasing any is never handed another frame, so the first
+         * drop is a warning rather than a debug line. */
+        int queued = atomic_load(&s->buffers_queued);
+        if (!bytesused || queued <= FFMAX(s->buffers / 8, 1)) {
+            if (bytesused && !s->frames_dropped)
+                av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Dropping frames: the consumer "
+                       "holds %d of %d capture buffers, and the rest stay "
+                       "queued so capture continues.\n",
+                       s->buffers - queued - 1, s->buffers);
+            else
+                av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "Dropping a frame: %s.\n",
+                       bytesused ? "too few buffers left queued"
+                                 : "the buffer holds no usable data");
+            s->frames_dropped++;
+            res = enqueue_buffer(s, &buf);
+            return res < 0 ? res : FFERROR_REDO;
+        }
+
+        res = drm_prime_wrap_buffer(ctx, pkt, buf.index);
+        if (res < 0)
+            return res;
+
+        pkt->pts = buf_ts.tv_sec * INT64_C(1000000) + buf_ts.tv_usec;
+        convert_timestamp(ctx, &pkt->pts);
+        return pkt->size;
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* Image is at s->buff_start[buf.index] */
     if (atomic_load(&s->buffers_queued) == FFMAX(s->buffers / 8, 1)) {
         /* when we start getting low on queued buffers, fall back on copying data */
@@ -694,8 +891,14 @@ static void mmap_close(struct video_data *s)
      */
     v4l2_ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_STREAMOFF, &type);
     for (i = 0; i < s->buffers; i++) {
-        v4l2_munmap(s->buf_start[i], s->buf_len[i]);
+        if (s->dmabuf_fd) {
+            if (s->dmabuf_fd[i] >= 0)
+                close(s->dmabuf_fd[i]);
+        } else {
+            v4l2_munmap(s->buf_start[i], s->buf_len[i]);
+        }
     }
+    av_freep(&s->dmabuf_fd);
     av_freep(&s->buf_start);
     av_freep(&s->buf_len);
 }
@@ -871,6 +1074,108 @@ static int device_try_init(AVFormatContext *ctx,
     return ret;
 }
 
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+/**
+ * Describe the negotiated format as a DRM PRIME layer and create the frames
+ * context the frames carry. The plane layout is the driver's: a line can be
+ * padded beyond the width, which the frame dimensions do not show.
+ */
+static int drm_prime_init(AVFormatContext *ctx)
+{
+    struct video_data *s = ctx->priv_data;
+    struct v4l2_format fmt = { .type = s->buf_type };
+    const AVPixFmtDescriptor *desc;
+    AVHWFramesContext *frames;
+    enum AVPixelFormat sw_fmt = AV_PIX_FMT_NONE;
+    uint32_t drm_fmt = 0;
+    unsigned int bytesperline, sizeimage;
+    int i, ret;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(drm_prime_formats); i++) {
+        if (drm_prime_formats[i].v4l2_fmt == s->pixelformat) {
+            drm_fmt = drm_prime_formats[i].drm_fmt;
+            sw_fmt  = drm_prime_formats[i].sw_fmt;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (!drm_fmt) {
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "The capture format %s has no DRM PRIME "
+               "equivalent.\n", av_fourcc2str(s->pixelformat));
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+    }
+
+    if (v4l2_ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_G_FMT, &fmt) < 0) {
+        ret = AVERROR(errno);
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "ioctl(VIDIOC_G_FMT): %s\n", av_err2str(ret));
+        return ret;
+    }
+    if (s->multiplanar) {
+        if (fmt.fmt.pix_mp.num_planes != 1) {
+            av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "DRM PRIME output supports one memory "
+                   "plane, the driver uses %u.\n", fmt.fmt.pix_mp.num_planes);
+            return AVERROR_PATCHWELCOME;
+        }
+        bytesperline = fmt.fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].bytesperline;
+        sizeimage    = fmt.fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].sizeimage;
+    } else {
+        bytesperline = fmt.fmt.pix.bytesperline;
+        sizeimage    = fmt.fmt.pix.sizeimage;
+    }
+
+    /* A semi-planar format in one buffer: the CbCr plane starts right after
+     * the last luma line, and its line holds two bytes per chroma site. */
+    desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(sw_fmt);
+    s->drm_layer.format                  = drm_fmt;
+    s->drm_layer.nb_planes               = av_pix_fmt_count_planes(sw_fmt);
+    s->drm_layer.planes[0].object_index  = 0;
+    s->drm_layer.planes[0].offset        = 0;
+    s->drm_layer.planes[0].pitch         = bytesperline;
+    if (s->drm_layer.nb_planes > 1) {
+        s->drm_layer.planes[1].object_index = 0;
+        s->drm_layer.planes[1].offset       = (ptrdiff_t)bytesperline * s->height;
+        s->drm_layer.planes[1].pitch        = bytesperline * 2 >> desc->log2_chroma_w;
+    }
+
+    /* A buffer is complete when it holds the driver's image size, which
+     * counts the padding the packed frame size does not. */
+    s->frame_size = sizeimage;
+
+    ret = av_hwdevice_ctx_create(&s->device_ref, AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_DRM,
+                                 s->drm_device, NULL, 0);
+    if (ret < 0) {
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Cannot open DRM device %s: %s\n",
+               s->drm_device, av_err2str(ret));
+        return ret;
+    }
+
+    s->frames_ref = av_hwframe_ctx_alloc(s->device_ref);
+    if (!s->frames_ref)
+        return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+    frames            = (AVHWFramesContext *)s->frames_ref->data;
+    frames->format    = AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME;
+    frames->sw_format = sw_fmt;
+    frames->width     = s->width;
+    frames->height    = s->height;
+
+    ret = av_hwframe_ctx_init(s->frames_ref);
+    if (ret < 0) {
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Cannot initialise the DRM PRIME frames "
+               "context: %s\n", av_err2str(ret));
+        return ret;
+    }
+
+    av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_VERBOSE, "DRM PRIME output: %s as %s, %u bytes per line.\n",
+           av_fourcc2str(s->pixelformat), av_get_pix_fmt_name(sw_fmt), bytesperline);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void drm_prime_uninit(struct video_data *s)
+{
+    av_buffer_unref(&s->frames_ref);
+    av_buffer_unref(&s->device_ref);
+}
+#endif
+
 static int v4l2_read_probe(const AVProbeData *p)
 {
     if (av_strstart(p->filename, "/dev/video", NULL))
@@ -892,6 +1197,21 @@ static int v4l2_read_header(AVFormatContext *ctx)
     if (!st)
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
 
+    if (s->drm_prime) {
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+        /* libv4l2 converts in its own buffers, which cannot be exported. */
+        if (s->use_libv4l2) {
+            av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "DRM PRIME output cannot be combined "
+                   "with libv4l2.\n");
+            return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+        }
+#else
+        av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "DRM PRIME output needs libavdevice built "
+               "with libdrm.\n");
+        return AVERROR(ENOSYS);
+#endif
+    }
+
 #if CONFIG_LIBV4L2
     /* silence libv4l2 logging. if fopen() fails v4l2_log_file will be NULL
        and errors will get sent to stderr */
@@ -990,6 +1310,10 @@ static int v4l2_read_header(AVFormatContext *ctx)
      */
     if (codec_id != AV_CODEC_ID_NONE && ctx->video_codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_NONE)
         ctx->video_codec_id = codec_id;
+    /* The stream carries wrapped frames, whatever the capture format is, and
+     * stream probing opens the decoder this names. */
+    if (s->drm_prime)
+        ctx->video_codec_id = AV_CODEC_ID_WRAPPED_AVFRAME;
 
     if ((res = av_image_check_size(s->width, s->height, 0, ctx)) < 0)
         goto fail;
@@ -1004,6 +1328,11 @@ static int v4l2_read_header(AVFormatContext *ctx)
         s->frame_size = av_image_get_buffer_size(st->codecpar->format,
                                                  s->width, s->height, 1);
 
+#if CONFIG_LIBDRM
+    if (s->drm_prime && (res = drm_prime_init(ctx)) < 0)
+        goto fail;
+#endif
+
     if ((res = mmap_init(ctx)) ||
         (res = mmap_start(ctx)) < 0)
             goto fail;
@@ -1011,25 +1340,39 @@ static int v4l2_read_header(AVFormatContext *ctx)
     s->top_field_first = first_field(s);
 
     st->codecpar->codec_type = AVMEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO;
-    st->codecpar->codec_id = codec_id;
-    if (codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_RAWVIDEO)
-        st->codecpar->codec_tag =
-            avcodec_pix_fmt_to_codec_tag(st->codecpar->format);
-    else if (codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264) {
